    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0308" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg224"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beaupré to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1903</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> (Received November 6, 1903, 5 p.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Fourth, 5 p.m. Confidential. I have been shown telegram from reliable source in
                    Panama to the effect that Isthmus is preparing for secession and that
                    proclamation of independence may be expected soon. The particulars carefully
                    guarded, Reliable information hard <pb facs="0309" n="225" xml:id="pg225"/> to
                    obtain. This Government is evidently alarmed and troops are being sent to
                    Isthmus. Repeat telegrams of importance from United States consul-general. His
                    telegrams to me may be interfered with.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
